## The Queen (`story.ni:11371-11376`): her look is her only description,
## with the source's first-time tail; a greeting (the ruling) and then the
## source's line; the evidence counter is hers.

create the Queen
  aka her majesty, her royal majesty, royal majesty, majesty, queen, woman, lady, pale woman, entourage
  a person, proper
  pronouns she
  states: unmet, greeted
  counter evidence starts 0 between 0 and 7

  Her Royal Majesty is not a tall lady, and most of the time all you can see
  of her is a flash of golden crown or silver hair glimpsed between the
  shoulders of her entourage. But every now and then the shoulders part, and
  you get a good look at her: a pale, angry-looking woman with sharp,
  shrewish features. Her tiny face is almost lost within the explosion of
  jewel-encrusted brocade and lace that geysers up from the collar of her
  gown.

  after the player examining
    first time
      phrase queen-eyes-flash
  end after

  on the player talking
    refuse when the Queen is greeted: cant-get-near-the-queen
    phrase queen-greeting-stub
    change the Queen to greeted
  end on

  on the player showing
    refuse cant-get-near-the-queen
  end on

  on the player giving
    refuse cant-get-near-the-queen
  end on

  on the player touching
    refuse cant-get-near-the-queen
  end on

  on the player attacking
    refuse cant-get-near-the-queen
  end on

define phrase queen-eyes-flash
  Then, for just a moment, her gaze meets yours. Her stern expression never
  changes, but her eyes seem to flash a warning. I'm watching you, she seems
  to say. Do not cross me.
end phrase

define phrase cant-get-near-the-queen
  With so many people crowding around trying to get the Queen's attention,
  you can't even get near her.
end phrase

define phrase queen-greeting-stub
  (TODO during play-testing — the Queen's greeting, and nothing more: one
  exchange across the throne, the only words she gives Jacqueline all night.
  The Queen is not ruled to see her; she judges the claim. David's lines.)
end phrase

